  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A new module `crates/cl/src/cl/transform.rs` with three sub-files (`transform_rotary.rs`, `transform_mirror.rs`, `transform_climb.rs`). `camcraft-app` re-exports it as `app::cl::transform`.\n- `translate(tp, [dx, dy, dz])` shifts every move, arc center, canned cycle, compensated span and edge break.\n- `transform_xy(tp, tx, ty, angle_deg, pivot)` turns the path in XY about a pivot and then shifts it. Nesting (#2166) can call it directly.\n- `rotate_about_axis(tp, RotaryAxis::A | B, origin, angle_deg, chord_tol)` turns the path about X or Y. Each move states the turned tool axis. Arcs become chords at `chord_tol`.\n- `mirror_plane(tp, MirrorPlane, MirrorMode)` mirrors the path across a vertical plane.\n  - `GeometricMirror` gives the exact mirror image: G2 <-> G3 and G41 <-> G42.\n  - `PreserveClimb(PassFamily)` mirrors and then runs each pass backwards between its entry and its retract. The lead-out becomes the lead-in. The arcs keep their original G2/G3, and the compensated spans keep their original side.\n- `TransformError` names each refusal: `ThreadCycle`, `ProbeTouch`, `RotaryMove`, `TiltedMove`, `PlasmaCut`, `VerticalArc`, `CannedCycleTilt`, `HorizontalMirrorPlane`, `TiltedMirrorPlane`, `BadInput`, `NotReversible(why)`.\n- The decisions are in `docs/decisions/3011-cl-transforms.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThis is new work. The codebase had no shared transform for toolpaths. Patterns, mirror folders and nesting need one.\n\n## Design\n\n- All four transforms use one map, `p -> M p + t`, with `M` orthogonal.\n- An arc keeps its plane only when `M` maps the plane normal exactly onto plus or minus itself. Its turn direction flips when `det(M)` times that sign is negative. This one rule gives the G2/G3 swap under a mirror. It also finds the XZ / YZ arcs that a transform cannot keep.\n- Moves, arc centers and cycles snap to the 1 um lattice. Edge-break polylines do not snap, because a snap would move framed caps off orthonormal.\n- `PreserveClimb` accepts only contour, profile and chamfer paths. It refuses these by name:\n  - a helical ramp, adaptive clearing, multi-pass roughing and other families;\n  - a ramp or helical entry;\n  - a level change without a retract;\n  - a cut before the first pass or after the last pass;\n  - a link that is not on the clearance plane.\n\n## Tests (pins)\n\nAll 20 tests are in `crates/cl/src/cl/transform_tests.rs` and `transform_mirror_tests.rs` (`cargo test -p camcraft-cl --lib transform`):\n\n- `translate_shifts_every_record_to_the_micron`, `translate_refuses_a_non_finite_offset`\n- `transform_xy_turns_a_quarter_about_the_pivot_then_shifts`, `transform_xy_at_thirty_degrees_is_micron_accurate`, `transform_xy_refuses_a_vertical_arc_it_cannot_keep`\n- `rotate_about_a_turns_the_point_and_states_the_axis`, `rotate_about_b_flattens_arcs_within_the_chord_tolerance`, `rotate_about_an_axis_by_zero_is_the_identity`, `rotate_about_an_axis_refuses_a_tilted_canned_cycle`\n- `every_transform_refuses_thread_cycles_probe_touches_and_c_moves`\n- `geometric_mirror_swaps_g2_g3_and_g41_g42`, `geometric_mirror_on_a_diagonal_plane_is_micron_accurate`, `mirror_refuses_horizontal_and_tilted_planes`, `mirror_refuses_tilted_moves`\n- `preserve_climb_reverses_the_pass_between_entry_and_retract`, `preserve_climb_reverses_two_depths_linked_on_the_clearance_plane`, `preserve_climb_refuses_a_helical_entry`, `preserve_climb_refuses_clearing_families_by_name`, `preserve_climb_refuses_a_cut_before_the_first_pass`, `preserve_climb_refuses_a_level_change_without_a_retract`\n\nBefore the fix, the pins did not compile (`translate`, `mirror_plane`, `TransformError` ... did not exist).\n\nMutation checks: I removed each guard, ran the pins (all red), and restored the guard (green):\n\n- the G2/G3 flip: 3 pins red\n- the G41/G42 swap: 2 pins red\n- the side restore in the climb reversal: 1 pin red\n- the probe refusal: 1 pin red\n- the refusal of a cut before the first pass: 1 pin red\n- the horizontal-plane refusal: 1 pin red\n- the pass reversal: 2 pins red\n- the tilted-cycle refusal: 1 pin red\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green on a273ee018: 1077 steps, 0 failed, clippy included. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-cl --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No existing code calls the module yet.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No caller exists yet: patterns, mirror folders and nesting (#2166) will use it.\n- No posted G-code goes through a transformed path in this PR.\n- The framed edge-break caps under a turn and under a mirror are not pinned by a test.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n#3046 adds a line to the module list of `crates/cl/src/cl/mod.rs` (the same file, but a different line). The PR that merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: CL toolpath transforms: translate, XY turn, A/B axis turn and vertical-plane mirror (G2/G3 and G41/G42 swap, or a climb-preserving pass reversal), with named refusals.\n\nFixes #3011\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
